sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch03-24> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch03-24--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch03-24--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch03-24: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.77" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.773"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.78"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The stated evidence is ponderosa ring width, and those series are openly archived at far higher replication than the few trees Thompson smoothed. Standard spectral tests can accept or reject a stable 150-year line. Discriminating power stays moderate because century smoothing and red noise can imitate a long cycle, and because moisture rather than temperature was an inference from the regional climate rather than a separate measurement." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: On Arizona ponderosa ring-width chronologies, compare a red-noise spectrum of the raw series and of 100-year smoothed means against a stable peak near 150 years over roughly 1390–1910, then repeat the test on an independent summer-drought reconstruction. A significant, stable 150-year peak would support the claim; a featureless continuum, or a peak that appears only after century smoothing, would refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "A 500-year window contains only about three cycles, and 100-year smoothing can impose a smooth wave.", "Ring width mixes moisture, temperature and stand dynamics.", "The gridded drought product used here is densest after 1700, so the early part of Thompson's interval rests mainly on the ring measurements." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch03-24--grok--dataset-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch03-24--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch03-24 by Grok 4.7: 0.85" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.85"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch03-24--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch03-24> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch03-24--grok--operationalizability> .
